and document utilities. All processing happens locally. Feedback welcome.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;OPTIMIZED FOR NOTION: &lt;a href="https://rebel-nurse-a44.notion.site/How-to-Utilize-AI-Not-Just-Use-It-The-AI-Utilization-Guide-36f38a21a4b880e0ae89fda867a4b75e?pvs=74" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;How to Utilize AI&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Fundamentals of Utilizing AI
&lt;/h2&gt;




&lt;p&gt;When using AI, people often run into two distinct experiences, information overload or putting in a question and getting an answer back. Leaving the learning experience to an afterthought. In today’s society, since AI is being pushed more and more in classrooms and workplaces, learning to use AI is becoming paramount to one’s success. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, what separates a user of AI from someone who utilizes AI in their workflows?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How they interact with AI. In order to utilize AI you need to understand how it works on a fundamental level. So, here’s the abridged version.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  How AI Works on A Fundamental Level
&lt;/h3&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fjk6f7h8p95u7vk0d65cs.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fjk6f7h8p95u7vk0d65cs.png" alt=" " width="735" height="751"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;VECTOR DATABASE&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Vectoring
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI uses an extraordinary amount of data! Billions even trillions of tokens or data points being used and analyzed over fractions of a second. The way this data interacts with itself uses a concept called vectoring. As pictured above the difference between a traditional data table you would’ve seen in high school is that every piece of data in a vector space has a geometric “distance” from another piece of data across hundreds or thousands of invisible dimensions. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI is then able to use these coordinates to perform complex calculations and formulate responses to user queries at incredible speeds. The overall process in practice is similar to searching for something through a search engine.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here’s an example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;“The boy asked his mother for a few dollars to go to the ___”&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In your head most likely you finished that sentence with “store”, though why is that? As a human you used your past experiences, context clues, and intuition to come to that conclusion. Though AI [Artificial Intelligence] is just that artificial. So, as AI was being developed Engineers needed to replicate that ability which is where vectoring is needed. You also have a vector database in your mind even if you haven’t realized it. You know “store” is closer to “house” than “cat” because of their relation via “building”.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F9lz87uqcj4m4lu8t2z2i.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F9lz87uqcj4m4lu8t2z2i.png" alt=" " width="612" height="459"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CLOCKS SET&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Why Do We Need New Models
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The image above represents a model. The time is set and won’t change. When a model is created, without going into immense detail, it resembles a wall of clocks with set times. That training data can no longer be changed though, data can be supplied to the model. Take the concept of RAG (retrieval augmented generation) users are able to create data stores that they supply to an AI model. The AI will then check itself against the data provided. So, as new research, data, and technology releases older models become outdated, requiring a new set of clocks, training data, to be created in order for the model itself to be updated. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Training data is not the main reason we get new models so often, though. The primary reason labs train entirely new models is to improve their reasoning capabilities, efficacy, and architecture.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Take Anthropics Claude model and Google's Nano Banana they have very distinct differences in capabilities which lies with the organizations themselves. Most companies are very secretive about the research they conduct. Often paying researchers millions for their research capabilities and never publishing it to the public. With different training data and architecture we end up with hundreds of AI models that vary in performance, capabilities, and focus. Though there is one company that breaks the mold, more on them later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, now that you have a better understanding of how AI fundamentally works there are numerous subsets of AI Engineering but here are two that you need to know, and don’t worry you don’t need to be an engineer to understand it. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Context Engineering + Prompt Engineering
&lt;/h3&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  Context Engineering Part 1/2- The Prompt
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let’s create an imaginary coffee shop called, “Not Your Average Coffee” that sells unique coffees. In a week we are releasing an “Iced Cheerwine Espresso” containing Oat Milk, Cheerwine, and a shot of Espresso. It will release for $6.99 this Summer only starting June 12th. We need a paragraph to put on a flyer that draws new and returning customers, though we can’t write it all right now. So, let’s use AI!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let’s take a look at an example prompt:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create a paragraph that announces the release of the new “Iced Cheerwine Espresso” at my coffee shop. It’s only available for the summer though.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The above prompt is very similar to a prompt most newcomers to AI are likely to use. While it sounds good at first glance there are a few issues. Take a second and think about what could be wrong with this…. now I’ll show you! I plugged our exact prompt into Google’s Gemini AI, this is the result:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Summer just got a whole lot bolder. We are thrilled to introduce our newest seasonal creation, the &lt;strong&gt;Iced Cheerwine Espresso&lt;/strong&gt;! This limited-time beverage perfectly marries the legendary, sweet cherry effervescence of Cheerwine with our rich, freshly pulled espresso, served over ice for the ultimate warm-weather pick-me-up. It is the crisp, caffeinated twist your summer routine has been begging for.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Don't wait to grab a cup—just like the season, this exclusive flavor profile will disappear when summer ends! What day are you thinking of adding this to the menu?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Horrible right? It’s missing a few things such as:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Price&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Ingredients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Day of Release (see how it asked a clarifying question at the end? More on that later.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Name of Our Coffee Shop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The reason for this is the lack of context, some people believe AI to be this all-knowing force though we know it’s not because we know how it works! It may know about your coffee shop it can even search your website for more information if need be. Though it needs access to that data and unless you give it that data it won’t have it. There are a few cool ways to give an AI the relevant context needed though let’s stick to the basics, refining your prompt.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here’s a better version of the prompt we used, I’ll highlight everything that's changed for you in green.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I own a coffee shop called, “Not Your Average Coffee” and we have a new exciting coffee the “Iced Cheerwine Espresso” containing a shot of Espresso, Cheerwine, and Oat Milk. The coffee will release for the Summer only, on June 12th for $6.99. Create a paragraph that I can use to promote this new coffee, include a disclaimer for people who may be allergic to nuts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the result:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Get ready to spark your summer with a truly bold flavor collision! Starting &lt;strong&gt;June 12th&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Not Your Average Coffee&lt;/em&gt; is dropping our exclusive, limited-run seasonal sensation: the &lt;strong&gt;Iced Cheerwine Espresso&lt;/strong&gt;. We are taking the legendary, cherry-forward fizz of Carolinas' own Cheerwine and layering it with a rich, bold shot of espresso, all smoothed out with a creamy pour of oat milk over ice. It’s bubbly, complex, and exactly the refreshing kick you need to beat the heat for just &lt;strong&gt;$6.99&lt;/strong&gt;. This unique creation is here for the summer only, so grab yours before it’s gone!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please Note:&lt;/strong&gt; While this beverage is crafted with oat milk, our shop handles tree nuts and other allergens. If you have a severe nut allergy, please inform our baristas before ordering so we can take extra precautions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Immediately the result is much better than our original result. When given the correct context an AI’s ability to give a satisfactory output increases drastically. Ultimately saving you money, compute, and time when delegating a task to AI. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;


  Context Engineering Part 2/2- The Chat
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In addition to the type of prompt that you pass in managing your chats are very important. Most people know that when you enter an AI’s website such as Claude or Gemini you are greeted by some variation of “Hello, [Your Name]” indicating that you’ve begun a new chat. Another way to begin a new chat is to manually start a new chat, something that many people don’t do organically.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Think of chats like conversations you may have with your friends. I’ll break this down into a Conversation A and Conversation B format.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conversation A&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;Topics: Sports, Cooking, Cars, Yesterdays Dinner, How to Ride a Bike, and a Shopping List&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conversation B&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;Topics: Looking for an apartment, favorite decor pieces, and neighborhoods&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;Both conversations I’m sure turned out to be a great time though there's a distinct difference in theme and topic. Let’s say at this point it’s been an A + B conversation. In order to add a third person into the conversation, person C would need significantly more context to participate in conversation A than conversation B. Making onboarding significantly harder. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now back to our two friends A and B, in conversation A if you asked someone a question then they would think about the whole conversation before giving you an answer. The issue with that is that in real conversations, you would ask a large amount of clarifying questions and would go back and forth trying to remember which parts of the conversation are relevant to the question asked. In a conversation with AI all of that extra processing can end up costing more than you bargained for, especially in the workplace. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Whilst in conversation B the context of the conversation is very easy to understand and be onboarded to. You should treat your chats with AI very similarly to conversation B for 90% of everyday tasks. If you are working on a larger project that spans numerous chats, topics, and context there are more advanced tactics you can use but that is not in scope for this article. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;


  Prompt Engineering Part 1/1 - Tailoring the Response
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tailoring the response begins at the…..you guessed it prompt! Prompt Engineering consists of a number of different concepts aimed at making sure your prompts are as effective as possible. The role of a Prompt Engineer is one that comes with a $100,000 salary attached and while I can’t shove all of that knowledge in this article, here are the 6 core principles that will take your prompting to the next level.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Principle 1: Be Specific&lt;/strong&gt; – Avoid vague requests. Narrow down the possibilities by adding explicit constraints like target audience, purpose, format, and length to eliminate generic default responses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Principle 2: Provide Context&lt;/strong&gt; – Give the AI situational, goal-oriented, or constraint-based background info (such as who you are, who the audience is, and what success looks like) to shape a highly relevant interpretation of the task. More on this in the sections on Context Engineering above!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Principle 3: Define the Format&lt;/strong&gt; – Explicitly specify how you want the output structured (e.g., as numbered lists, comparison tables, or a simple paragraph) to ensure the result is immediately usable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Principle 4: Assign a Role&lt;/strong&gt; – Giving an AI a role such as “A kindhearted third-grade teacher looking to encourage his classroom before a big test”, allows it to understand the nuances required to create a relevant response. If you remember in the responses we looked at for our coffee shop example the AI took on a response and vibe of its own choosing so we didn’t assign it a role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Principle 5: Use Examples (Few-Shot Prompting)&lt;/strong&gt; – Show rather than just tell. Providing one or more high-quality examples of the exact style, tone, or pattern you want allows the AI to mimic it consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Principle 6: Request Reasoning (Chain-of-Thought)&lt;/strong&gt; – Ask the model to "think step-by-step" for complex tasks. Breaking a problem down into intermediate reasoning steps significantly improves accuracy and makes logical errors easier to spot and fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here’s an example prompt revisiting our favorite coffee shop, Not Your Average Coffee and all 6 principles, see if you can spot them all:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My coffee shop, Not Your Average Coffee, is releasing a new coffee for the Summer starting June 12th through August 21st! An “Iced Cheerwine Espresso” that retails at $6.99. You are to take on the persona of a welcoming store clerk inviting new and returning customers to try out this new coffee. The goal is to increase sales during this time period and generate an extra 5% revenue which will mean we need to sell 9,543 of these new coffees. Your response should consist of a paragraph to use in an Instagram caption as well as one liners that I can put on a flyer. Here’s an example (we’re reusing our earlier response):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;“Get ready to spark your summer with a truly bold flavor collision! Starting &lt;strong&gt;June 12th&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Not Your Average Coffee&lt;/em&gt; is dropping our exclusive, limited-run seasonal sensation: the &lt;strong&gt;Iced Cheerwine Espresso&lt;/strong&gt;. We are taking the legendary, cherry-forward fizz of Carolinas' own Cheerwine and layering it with a rich, bold shot of espresso, all smoothed out with a creamy pour of oat milk over ice. It’s bubbly, complex, and exactly the refreshing kick you need to beat the heat for just &lt;strong&gt;$6.99&lt;/strong&gt;. This unique creation is here for the summer only, so grab yours before it’s gone!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please Note:&lt;/strong&gt; While this beverage is crafted with oat milk, our shop handles tree nuts and other allergens. If you have a severe nut allergy, please inform our baristas before ordering so we can take extra precautions.”&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Explain your reasoning and thought process step-by-step in order to create a framework that can be replicated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here’s the response that we get: &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;


  Step-by-Step Framework &amp;amp; Thought Process
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To create a highly effective, repeatable promotional campaign, the content needs to be broken down into a strategic framework. This ensures that every piece of copy serves a specific psychological and logistical purpose to hit that 5% revenue milestone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is the step-by-step breakdown used to build your new assets:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;


  Step 1: Define the Core Hook &amp;amp; Identity
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Goal:&lt;/strong&gt; Stop the scroll on social media and grab attention immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Lean heavily into the unique, local identity of Cheerwine and the adventurous nature of your brand name (&lt;em&gt;Not Your Average Coffee&lt;/em&gt;). The contrast of bubbly, sweet cherry soda and rich espresso is an exciting "flavor collision" that needs to be front and center.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;


  Step 2: Establish the Value Proposition &amp;amp; Logistics
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Goal:&lt;/strong&gt; Give the customer the exact details they need to make a purchase decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Clearly state the price (&lt;strong&gt;$6.99&lt;/strong&gt;), the exact date range (&lt;strong&gt;June 12th – August 21st&lt;/strong&gt;), and the flavor profile (cherry fizz, bold espresso, creamy oat milk). Highlighting the premium ingredients justifies the price point and sets taste expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;


  Step 3: Manufacture Urgency &amp;amp; Scarcity
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Goal:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive immediate action so customers don't "procrastinate" their visit, helping you hit that &lt;strong&gt;9,543-unit goal&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Use time-bound language like "limited-run," "exclusive," and "summer-only." This triggers FOMO (Fear Of Missing Out) and encourages repeat visits during the brief window the drink is available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;


  Step 4: Craft the Call to Action (CTA) &amp;amp; Operational Safety
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Goal:&lt;/strong&gt; Tell the customer exactly what to do next while managing store transparency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct them straight to the counter. Including a clear allergen warning builds trust and keeps your baristas and customers safe without dampening the excitement of the promotion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;


  Instagram Caption
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Summer just got a major flavor upgrade! Starting &lt;strong&gt;June 12th&lt;/strong&gt;, Not Your Average Coffee is officially dropping our exclusive, limited-run seasonal sensation: the &lt;strong&gt;Iced Cheerwine Espresso&lt;/strong&gt;! We’re bringing you a true Southern collision of flavors, pairing the legendary, sweet cherry-forward fizz of Carolinas' favorite Cheerwine with a rich, bold shot of premium espresso—all perfectly smoothed out with a creamy pour of oat milk over ice. It’s bubbly, complex, wonderfully refreshing, and the ultimate way to beat the heat for just &lt;strong&gt;$6.99&lt;/strong&gt;. This unique creation is staying cool on our menu only through &lt;strong&gt;August 21st&lt;/strong&gt;, so make it your new summer ritual before it disappears! &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please Note:&lt;/strong&gt; While this seasonal beverage is crafted with oat milk, our shop handles tree nuts and other allergens. If you have a severe nut allergy, please inform our baristas before ordering so we can take extra precautions to keep you safe!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;


  Flyer One-Liners
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;"The South’s favorite fizz meets your daily buzz: Try the Iced Cheerwine Espresso!"&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;"Not Your Average Summer. Not Your Average Espresso. June 12th – Aug 21st."&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;"Bold espresso. Sweet cherry fizz. Creamy oat milk. Summer in a cup for $6.99."&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;"Beat the heat with a Southern classic, reinvented. Limited time only!"&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;"Caffeine meets Cheerwine—spark your summer starting June 12th!"&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Immediately you’re able to see all of the issues we had with the former results are solved. When you provide an AI with the concepts we talked about above there’s a lot less guessing and we don’t waste energy, money, and time on bad queries.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Choosing any combination of these principles will increase your efficiency and increase your ability to utilize AI, not just use it. Though I highly encourage you to take time and research these principles further to the point of understanding and being able to apply these principles. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Utilizing AI vs Using AI
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The final thing we need to learn in order to understand how to utilize AI on a fundamental level is the difference between using and utilizing. If you don’t immediately know the difference that's okay here are the definitions for both:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Use -&lt;/strong&gt; To employ something for its &lt;strong&gt;intended purpose&lt;/strong&gt; or standard function. It is the most common, general term for consuming, operating, or executing a task with an object, tool, or resource.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Utilize -&lt;/strong&gt; To find a &lt;strong&gt;practical, profitable, or novel use&lt;/strong&gt; for something, often turning a resource toward a purpose it wasn't originally designed for, or maximizing its efficiency. It implies strategy, adaptation, or extracting value from something that might otherwise go to waste.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Utilizing AI requires one to understand how AI works on a fundamental level, creativity to employ AI into your workflows, an understanding of frameworks and concepts that boost efficiency, and finally a growth mindset. While using AI is an experience familiar to everyone. Maybe it was forced on you through Google’s AI search, your job, or the fact that it is the topic of every conversation nowadays. You used it for a project at school or work and you got all the answers to your questions but left more confused than ever, without having learned anything. It’s frustrating when a quick 30 minute project turns into an hour of failed queries and yelling at a machine that doesn’t have feelings. “You are very correct, I’ll change that now” is the response you get to the 5th piece of irrelevant information it gives you. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let’s do another exercise using Person A and Person B.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Person A&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;Person A is a Teacher with a newborn baby and needs to grade his students’ test by the end of the evening. He’s exhausted and decides to &lt;strong&gt;use&lt;/strong&gt; AI to grade the papers. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fast forward a few hours and he’s juggling a crying baby and the frustrating amalgamation of 1’s and 0’s on his screen. Leading to him giving up and crying himself to sleep.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Person B&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;Person B is a Teacher with a newborn baby and needs to grade her students’ test by the end of the evening. She’s exhausted and decides to &lt;strong&gt;utilize&lt;/strong&gt; AI to grade the papers. She’s read this article and proceeds to give examples of papers she’s graded in the past. She specifies the class, grade, and current topics of the papers to be graded.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;She’s able to get a quick nap in as the baby has fallen asleep and the AI workflow she’s using is autonomous so, by the time she wakes up it’s finished.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;Both using the same AI to complete different experiences. This is only one of the few examples of what can happen when using AI vs utilizing AI.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;


  The Dangers of Using AI To Complete Complex Tasks You Know Nothing About
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine you’re not a teacher and you are trying to fulfill the role of Person A. You don’t have the knowledge or training needed to effectively complete this task with or without AI. AI as we know is not all powerful and while it has and will continue to improve by leaps and bounds it is prone to hallucinate and make up information to keep you the user satisfied with the service provided. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It grades the papers using solely its data it was trained on or can access via the internet, not your class curriculum, though you don’t know the difference, the AI returns papers graded on a College level versus your eleventh grade class. Their grades drop significantly but the issue isn’t caught until it’s too late.  Now you end up fired from your job. While this is an extreme case it proves how one small use of AI without relevant knowledge can have real consequences. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now imagine a business owner trying to use AI for legal advice, a cook using AI to create an advertisement, a software engineer who uses AI to create an app without knowledge on security, etc. all of these people using AI instead of utilizing it can create very dangerous consequences.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI does not replace expertise but enhances it. Take the time to learn about the basics of what you’re trying to do and the output you’re looking for, don’t take shortcuts without the knowledge needed to make it effective. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now that you’ve learned the fundamentals of utilizing AI, I'm going to show you two different ways to get started.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Cloud vs Local Usage
&lt;/h2&gt;




&lt;p&gt;Now that you know how to utilize AI what are some of the ways that you can use AI? Whether you choose to use it through the web, an app, a third party application, voice, text, etc. whatever the medium you are connecting to an AI company’s servers and resources are being used and your data is being shared. For a lot of people whether for personal or legal reasons, a personal reason may be the negative devastating effects AI data centers are having in rural communities and a legal reason may be the fact that you are a lawyer and cannot put personal information into an AI due to confidentiality. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What are the solutions available to you? We’ll be taking a look at “Local Usage”. Local usage is means downloading an AI model directly to your computer and using your own computer's resources to host the model, instead of using a cloud-based model that connects to a server and company data center.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let’s look at a side by side comparison of Cloud vs Local usage to give you an idea of the pros and cons of each use case.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud Usage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Pros:&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Quicker Queries:&lt;/strong&gt; Backed by enterprise-grade hardware (like clusters of advanced H100 or TPU chips), cloud models can process complex requests and generate high-token outputs much faster than standard consumer hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Automatic Access to Cutting-Edge Models:&lt;/strong&gt; You instantly get to use the latest, largest, and most capable models without needing to manage updates, configurations, or installations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Zero Hardware Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt; It works perfectly on almost any device—whether it’s a high-end desktop, a lightweight laptop, or a smartphone—because the heavy lifting is done remotely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Cons:&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Data Privacy &amp;amp; Confidentiality:&lt;/strong&gt; Your data is transmitted to external servers. For professionals handling proprietary code, legal documents, or sensitive client information, this can pose significant confidentiality risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Ongoing Costs:&lt;/strong&gt; High-volume use or access to premium tiers usually requires a monthly subscription or API pay-per-token fees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Internet Dependency:&lt;/strong&gt; If you lose your internet connection, you completely lose access to the AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Local Usage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Pros:&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Absolute Privacy &amp;amp; Security:&lt;/strong&gt; Your data never leaves your machine. This makes it the ideal choice for developers, researchers, or businesses working with confidential data or strict regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Offline Functionality:&lt;/strong&gt; Once downloaded, local models require zero internet access. You can run queries in remote locations, on a flight, or during network outages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Customization &amp;amp; No Censorship:&lt;/strong&gt; You have complete control over the system prompts, parameters, and fine-tuning. Local open-source models lack the rigid guardrails or forced behavioral adjustments often implemented by commercial cloud providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Cons:&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Hardware Intensive:&lt;/strong&gt; Running capable models smoothly demands robust local hardware, typically requiring a high-end GPU with significant VRAM (Video RAM). On standard consumer laptops, performance can be sluggish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Manual Maintenance:&lt;/strong&gt; You have to find, download, install, and update the models yourself using tools like Ollama or LM Studio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Model Size Limitations:&lt;/strong&gt; Consumer hardware can generally only run compressed or smaller-parameter models (e.g., 8B to 70B parameters), which may lack the broad, generalized knowledge base of massive cloud models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;Now that you know the pros and cons I encourage you to try them both! As I mentioned before there are a number of different use cases and you often will come across both, especially if you work in tech. As a lawyer, politician, health care professional, engineer, etc. you most likely aren’t able to use cloud AI in your work due to legal or privacy issues so what most do is commission AI devices from hobbyist or download their own local AI here's how to do it! &lt;/p&gt;

